{
  "catalogue": {
    "sharedSelectionEntries": [
      {
        "profiles": [
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "name": "Terrain Name",
                "typeId": "aa90-71fa-e8fb-2ead",
                "$text": "Lightly Forested Woods"
              },
              {
                "name": "Terrain Type",
                "typeId": "6451-8783-55cc-50f6",
                "$text": "Woods, Forest, Light Cover"
              },
              {
                "name": "Terrain Special Rules",
                "typeId": "85de-dbe8-2f67-10ea",
                "$text": "A Model or Unit within this Terrain Feature has +1 to their DEF against any Ballistic Skill-related attacks. Any Model or unit that fights in Melee Combat in Lightly Forested Woods Terrain resolves all attacks at -1 Initiative."
              }
            ],
            "name": "Light Forested Woods",
            "typeId": "fed3-9148-5258-a028",
            "typeName": "Terrain Feature",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "d951-e092-f4d3-2ecc"
          }
        ],
        "type": "model",
        "import": true,
        "name": "Light Forested Woods",
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "3c0e-05db-6d9d-803e"
      },
      {
        "profiles": [
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "name": "Terrain Name",
                "typeId": "aa90-71fa-e8fb-2ead",
                "$text": "Densely Forested Woods"
              },
              {
                "name": "Terrain Type",
                "typeId": "6451-8783-55cc-50f6",
                "$text": "Forest, Woods, Medium Cover"
              },
              {
                "name": "Terrain Special Rules",
                "typeId": "85de-dbe8-2f67-10ea",
                "$text": "Any Ballistic Skill attacks that targets a model/unit inside this terrain feature, or a model/unit being targeted by mode/unit from within the the terrain feature, must be first resolved with an Intelligence Check, if they fail, they suffer a BS Modifier of -2 until the end of the attack. Any Model or unit that fights in Melee Combat in Densely Forested Woods Terrain resolves all attacks at -2 Initiative. \nMedium Cover: Provides a DEF Bonus of +2."
              }
            ],
            "name": "Densely Forested Woods",
            "typeId": "fed3-9148-5258-a028",
            "typeName": "Terrain Feature",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "e04d-68a6-6f46-6e4c"
          }
        ],
        "type": "model",
        "import": true,
        "name": "Densely Forested Wood",
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "87b8-62af-c1ca-db19"
      },
      {
        "profiles": [
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "$text": "Forest-World",
                "name": "Map Name",
                "typeId": "0639-cb4c-b4b7-7460"
              },
              {
                "$text": "Forests, Woods",
                "name": "Map Type",
                "typeId": "8105-e4c2-53a4-c814"
              },
              {
                "$text": "Due to the crowded canopy of the trees, all weapons with the Indirect Fire keyword lose Indirect Fire.",
                "name": "Map Special Rules",
                "typeId": "9ec7-70bb-e73b-28f9"
              }
            ],
            "name": "Forest-World",
            "typeId": "cd80-0960-0624-8eba",
            "typeName": "Map Feature",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "0722-7f08-34ad-c579"
          },
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "$text": "A Forest-World is often shrouded with giant trees, forming an impenetrable canopy that stretches for miles, even the most scarce area of trees has a scattering of medium to large sized trees.",
                "name": "Lore",
                "typeId": "8f51-2099-f67c-300e"
              }
            ],
            "name": "Forest-World",
            "typeId": "0d83-d584-6c16-6b6f",
            "typeName": "Lore",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "7d66-ecbf-c155-0b08"
          }
        ],
        "selectionEntries": [
          {
            "constraints": [
              {
                "type": "min",
                "value": 0,
                "field": "selections",
                "scope": "parent",
                "shared": true,
                "id": "ca07-0d20-c957-1957"
              },
              {
                "type": "max",
                "value": 1,
                "field": "selections",
                "scope": "parent",
                "shared": true,
                "id": "d110-8285-1375-62c2"
              }
            ],
            "profiles": [
              {
                "characteristics": [
                  {
                    "$text": "Forest-Worlds are usually dominated by great beasts that roam the planet, their roars and howls being carried by the winds rend the nerves of any poorly-trained survivor. However, some beasts are closer than one may think as stranglers are picked off as soon as they stray too far.",
                    "name": "Lore",
                    "typeId": "8f51-2099-f67c-300e"
                  }
                ],
                "name": "What Lurks in the Forest (Optionable)",
                "typeId": "0d83-d584-6c16-6b6f",
                "typeName": "Lore",
                "hidden": false,
                "id": "ef12-43eb-a26e-0a52"
              },
              {
                "characteristics": [
                  {
                    "$text": "A model or unit is that does not have line of sight to another friendly model/unit within 12 inches rolls a d6; if it is a unit, roll a d6 for each model. \n1: An unfortunate soul is picked off by a denizen of the forests. Remove a model from the unit.\n2-3: Noticeably shaken by the sounds of horrific creatures lurking in the undergrowth, they must take a suppression test. Do note: If this was rolled multiple times for a unit, only one test must be taken.\n4-5:They earn their nerve once more, seeing the beasts as nothing but mythos. Nothing else happens.\n6: The unit realizes they are lacking behind, and quickly pushes themselves forward. Make a normal movement action for free.Do note: If this was rolled multiple times for a unit, it is only done once.",
                    "name": "Description",
                    "typeId": "56ac-09e6-a6ce-498c"
                  }
                ],
                "name": "What Lurks in the Forest (Optionable)",
                "typeId": "db54-88f2-eb1c-6770",
                "typeName": "Abilities",
                "hidden": false,
                "id": "cb8f-7226-ce3a-f253"
              }
            ],
            "type": "upgrade",
            "import": true,
            "name": "What Lurks in the Forest (Optionable)",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "2ee6-d203-1fb0-4932"
          }
        ],
        "type": "model",
        "import": true,
        "name": "Forest-World",
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "7b4a-0f37-085d-fcef"
      },
      {
        "profiles": [
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "name": "Lore",
                "typeId": "8f51-2099-f67c-300e",
                "$text": "A City-Complex is often a vast, or at least rather large, grouping of well-kept advanced towns and cities within a great stretch of land. Filled with homes, businesses, production factories, and many other civilian businesses. Despite their calm and innocent nature, warfare has no bounds, and such places are found under assault."
              }
            ],
            "name": "City-Complex",
            "typeId": "0d83-d584-6c16-6b6f",
            "typeName": "Lore",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "4cce-9220-159e-92a9"
          },
          {
            "characteristics": [
              {
                "name": "Map Name",
                "typeId": "0639-cb4c-b4b7-7460",
                "$text": "City-Complex"
              },
              {
                "name": "Map Type",
                "typeId": "8105-e4c2-53a4-c814",
                "$text": "Urban, Destroyed Buildings/Undestroyed Buildings"
              },
              {
                "name": "Map Special Rules",
                "typeId": "9ec7-70bb-e73b-28f9",
                "$text": "With the advanced nature of City Complexes, forces are able to coordinate without hindrance. Ignore the-1 penalty from Reinforcement Reserves for the first time each round you bring a unit from Reinforcements."
              }
            ],
            "name": "City-Complex",
            "typeId": "cd80-0960-0624-8eba",
            "typeName": "Map Feature",
            "hidden": false,
            "id": "663a-e1e3-fc94-e7fb"
          }
        ],
        "type": "upgrade",
        "import": true,
        "name": "City-Complex",
        "hidden": false,
        "id": "906b-7dd5-065e-47b3"
