    "library": false,
    "id": "a440-393c-2e49-bac0",
    "name": "Terrain Features",
    "gameSystemId": "sys-3396-9326-565c-5fb6",
    "gameSystemRevision": 9,
    "revision": 5,
    "battleScribeVersion": 2.03,
    "type": "catalogue",
    "xmlns": "http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema",
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Light Fortification ",
        "id": "ea89-51f1-5569-b07e",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "This Fortification may be destroyed and when it is destroyed, use the table below on a d10 for every unit within. When this Fortification is destroyed, it is removed from play.\n\n1-3:All Models within this Fortification suffer 1 Damage; which can be saved; treated as whatever weapon type they can save against.\n4-6:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a fall back action away from the Fortification and must take a Suppression Test; losing an action for their next activation.\n7-9:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a standard movement action away from the Fortification; losing an action for their next activation.\n10: The Building holds together somehow! Instead of being destroyed, it is placed at 1 HP."
      },
      {
        "name": "Light Cover",
        "id": "25a9-ff6d-ef26-b2a6",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "Provides +1 DEF to a Unit within this Terrain Feature."
      },
      {
        "name": "Medium Cover",
        "id": "439a-9b6a-bd20-de21",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "Provides +2 DEF to a Unit within this Terrain Feature."
      },
      {
        "name": "Heavy Cover",
        "id": "b8cf-8f0c-f148-dbe3",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "Provides +3 DEF to a Unit within this Terrain Feature."
      },
      {
        "name": "Landing Pad",
        "id": "7fda-f9cc-66fe-6ca8",
        "hidden": false
      },
      {
        "name": "Battlements ",
        "id": "3b5c-2d12-59cb-61cd",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "Battlements are treated as an Access Point for their Building, meaning a unit inside the building can disembark onto the Battlements, or vice versa. Note that buildings without Transport Capacity that have battlements may still not be entered, although units can use their battlements.\n\n\nEnemy Units may also be placed onto Battlements if there is space and is a eligible move; even if the Building itself is embarked with a Friendly Unit."
      },
      {
        "name": "Firing Points",
        "id": "dd3b-6219-a2c1-7951",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "A Building with this special rule and a transport capacity can have it's embarked unit(s) perform shooting actions, measuring and drawing line of sight from any point on this model. They can do this even if there is an Enemy within Melee Range."
      },
      {
        "name": "Dangerous Terrain",
        "id": "c036-777d-bd6a-7456",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": ""
      },
      {
        "name": "Very Dangerous Terrain",
        "id": "1f60-bf59-5222-22fd",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "The Initiative Value of Units within this terrain feature is reduced to 1. \nCharges cannot be done through this terrain feature, even if you can clearly see the enemy unit and the move is eligible; you can only charge into units within Very Dangerous Terrain."
      },
      {
        "name": "Building Damage Table",
        "id": "2c56-15de-9e40-bcbe",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "1-3:Building Shaken: The Building and any Embarked units or units on the Building's Battlements can only fire Snap Shots until the end of the next turn.\n4:Structural Tremor: The Building and any Embarked units or units on the Building's Battlements can only fire Snap Shots until the end of its next turn. If the Building is occupied, the occupying unit suffers an additional D6 Strength 6 AP- Hits with the Ignores Cover special rule.\n5:Weapon Destroyed: One of the Building's weapons (chosen by the controlling player) is destroyed - including any combi- or built-in weapons. This can include Building upgrades that are weapons, such as Pintle Mounted weapons and missiles. Do not count single shot weapons that have already been used to attack. If a Building has no weapons left, treat this result as a Catastrophic Breach result instead.\n6:Catastrophic Breach: The Building and any Embarked units or units on the Building's Battlements may not make Shooting Attacks until the end of its next turn. No units may Embark or Disembark from the Building until the end of the controlling player's next turn. If the Building is occupied, the occupying unit suffers an additional 2D6 Strength 6 AP- Hits with the Ignores Cover special rule.\n7+:Total Collapse!: The Building is destroyed. All weapons and upgrades on the Building are destroyed. Each unit on the Battlements suffer 2D6 Strength 6 AP- Hits with the Ignores Cover special rule and must then immediately make a 6\" move in order to move off the Battlements are removed as casualties. If the Building is occupied , the occupying unit suffers 4D6 Strength 6 AP- Hits with the Ignores Cover special rule and must then immediately Disembark from the Building , performing an Emergency Disembarkation if necessary (survivors cannot Disembark to the Battlements). Any model that cannot Disembark are removed as casualties. Assuming they were not destroyed, units that were on the Battlements and those who have Disembarked must then take a Pinning test. The Building is then removed and replaced with an area of Ruins or a Crater roughly the same size if possible."
      },
      {
        "name": "Medium Fortification ",
        "id": "19ec-06bf-fd3e-e479",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "This Fortification may be destroyed and when it is destroyed, use the table below on a d10 for every unit within. When this Fortification is destroyed, it is removed from play.\n\n1-3:All Models within this Fortification suffer 1 Damage; which can be saved but the save is worsened by 1; treated as whatever weapon type they can save against.\n4-6:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a fall back action away from the Fortification and must take a Suppression Test, worsening the test result by 1; losing an action for their next activation.\n7-9:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a standard movement action away from the Fortification; losing an action for their next activation.\n10: The Building holds together somehow! Instead of being destroyed, it is placed at 1 HP."
      },
      {
        "name": "Heavy Fortication",
        "id": "5bbc-ad3a-1829-917b",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "This Fortification may be destroyed and when it is destroyed, use the table below on a d10 for every unit within. When this Fortification is destroyed, it is removed from play and in it's place, a Pile of Rubble Terrain Feature is left.\n\n1-3:All Models within this Fortification suffer 1 Damage; which cannot be saved.\n4-6:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a fall back action away from the Fortification and must take a Stunned Test, worsening the test by 1; losing an action for their next activation.\n7-9:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a standard movement action away from the Fortification; losing an action for their next activation.\n10: The Building holds together somehow! Instead of being destroyed, it is placed at 1 HP."
      },
      {
        "name": "Building Test",
        "id": "f4b7-e235-9fb4-67e9",
        "hidden": false,
        "description": "This Building may be destroyed and when it is destroyed, use the table below on a d10 for every unit within. When this Building is destroyed, it is removed from play and in it's place, a Pile of Rubble Terrain Feature is left.\n\n1-3:All Models within this Building suffer 1 Damage; which can be saved; treated as whatever weapon type they can save against.\n4-6:The Building is destroyed, all units within perform a fall back action away from the Fortification and must take a Suppression Test; losing an action for their next activation.\n7-9:The Fortification is destroyed, all units within perform a standard movement action away from the Fortification; losing an action for their next activation.\n10: The Building holds together somehow! Instead of being destroyed, it is placed at 1 HP."
      }
    ]
  }
}